      "text": "LocalRoute.ai | Founding Engineer (Infra &#x2F; Full-Stack) | NYC or REMOTE (US)<p>We’re an early-stage startup building a privacy-first AI routing layer for teams running multiple models across on-prem and hybrid environments.<p>The problem: AI workloads default to overpowered models and leak sensitive data because there’s no intelligent routing layer.<p>We’re looking for a founding engineer who enjoys systems-level problems, ambiguity, and owning architecture end-to-end. You’ll help design routing logic, policy enforcement, and developer-facing interfaces from the ground up.<p>Tech we’re working with &#x2F; around: backend services, model orchestration, infra, performance, privacy boundaries (stack flexible at this stage).<p>Location: NYC preferred, open to strong remote (US)\nStage: very early, YC-bound\nComp: equity (range depends on stage and fit)<p>Email: Team@localroute.ai\n(include a few lines on what you’ve built and what excites you)"
